meta {
  name: Download video
  type: http
  seq: 13
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/videos/{{videoId}}/download
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  Any member who can see the video, READY only. Each call uses **one unit of the club's download quota** and writes a `download_logs` row, both in one transaction. The response is a 5-minute presigned URL for the **original upload**. Storage sends it with `Content-Disposition: attachment`, so a browser saves the file instead of playing it. The disposition is part of the signature: change it and storage returns 403.

  | Status | Code | When |
  |---|---|---|
  | 200 | | download created and logged |
  | 403 | `QUOTA_EXCEEDED` | the club has no downloads left (see Get club quota) |
  | 404 | `VIDEO_NOT_FOUND` | you can't see this video |
  | 404 | `VIDEO_FILE_MISSING` | the original file is gone from storage; no quota is used |
  | 409 | `VIDEO_NOT_READY` | the video isn't READY |

  Example response:

  ```json
  {
    "download": {
      "url": "http://localhost:9000/raw-uploads/clubs/42c0a5d2-.../videos/4dce8038-.../original.mp4?X-Amz-...&X-Amz-Expires=300&response-content-disposition=attachment%3B%20filename%3D%22Two-minute%20demo%20%281080p%29.mp4%22%3B%20filename%2A%3DUTF-8%27%27...&X-Amz-Signature=...",
      "filename": "Two-minute demo (1080p).mp4",
      "sizeBytes": 297873717,
      "expiresAt": "2026-10-19T11:05:00.000Z"
    },
    "quota": { "limit": 100, "used": 1, "remaining": 99 }
  }
  ```

  Quota is used when the link is created, not when the file finishes downloading. Storage can't tell the API that a download completed, so this is the only point where it can be counted reliably.
}
